. lambessa. Due to the thinly whitish scaled dc O. oberthueri is also slightly similar to O. albomaculatus sp. nov. The latter is smaller and shows two whitish scaled areas in the basal and distal part of the dc.","","text","",""]]},"SF54":{"d":[["","ITA-IT","tdwg","native",""],["Italy","","text","native",""]]},"SFXCN":{"d":[["Distribution. China (Xinjiang).","","text","",""]]},"SX6QP":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"T3Y7K":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"T46D":{"d":[["China","","text","native",""]]},"T8QWN":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]},"TC7T":{"d":[["Neotropical(Venezuela)","","text","",""]]},"TC83":{"d":[["Neotropical(Bolivia)","","text","",""]]},"TRBGS":{"d":[["Distribution. Currently known only from Ea So NR, Dak Lak Province, Central Highlands of Vietnam (Figure 19).","","text","",""]]},"TZLZN":{"d":[["Sri Lanka","","text","",""]]},"V447M":{"d":[["China (Hainan)","","text","",""]]},"V4YKT":{"d":[["France","48144","mrgid","",""]]},"V552P":{"d":[["India","","text","",""]]},"V9RJW":{"d":[["Peru","","text","",""]]},"WPSH":{"d":[["peninsular Malaysia (Klang Gates, Selangor)","","text","",""]]},"WXCP":{"d":[["","GRC","tdwg","",""]]},"YNQJ":{"d":[["","ATP","tdwg","",""],["","NZN","tdwg","",""],["","NZS","tdwg","",""]]}}